WEBVTT

00:01:28.746 --> 00:01:33.246
our ability to remember things
doesn't seem very impressive at all.

00:01:33.496 --> 00:01:36.746
Nineteenth-century psychologist
Herman Ebbinghaus

00:01:36.788 --> 00:01:39.871
demonstrated that we normally forget
40% of new material

00:01:39.913 --> 00:01:41.538
within the first 20 minutes,

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:45.038
a phenomenon known
as “the forgetting curve”.

00:01:45.163 --> 00:01:49.163
But this loss can be prevented
through memory consolidation,

00:01:49.204 --> 00:01:51.663
the process by which
information is moved

00:01:51.704 --> 00:01:57.038
from our fleeting short-term memory
to our more durable long-term memory.

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:00.621
This consolidation occurs with the help
of a major part of the brain,